┌ lazyflk ─ host ready · LAN 10.47.11.116 · boot service ok ───────────── demo ┐
│ ┌ volumes backup ─ minecraft-flk ──────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│ │ Copy volumes (default: all of the app's) to the backup dir, then prune   │ │
│ │ old copies                                                               │ │
│ │ · How the app is kept from writing comes from [flk.backup] in flk.toml   │ │
│ │   (see flk help --all): by default its machine is stopped for the copy   │ │
│ │   and started again; mode = "live" with pre/post hooks (e.g. save-off /  │ │
│ │   save-on) copies while it runs.                                         │ │
│ │ · Copies are sparse, and instant on XFS/btrfs when the backup dir shares │ │
│ │   … (flk help volumes backup)                                            │ │
│ │                                                                          │ │
│ │ app         [minecraft-flk▏                                            ] │ │
│ │             the app (-a); the selection's app by default                 │ │
│ │ ID|NAME...  [                                                          ] │ │
│ │ --to DIR    [                                                          ] │ │
│ │ --keep N    [                                                          ] │ │
├ │ --mode MODE [                                                          ] │─┤
│ │ --no-check  ‹ no ›                                                       │ │
│ │                                                                          │ │
│ │ $ flk -a minecraft-flk volumes backup                                    │ │
